[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "London System"]
[Variation "Rapport-Jobava System, Nb5 and c7"]
[ECO "D01"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,fork"]
[Themes "c7-square"]
[RefutedBy "1. d4 d5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. Bf4 c5 4. e3 Nc6 5. Nb5"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "against-us"]
[Opponent "5.Nb5"]
[Start "1. d4 d5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. Bf4"]

3... c5 $6 { Not a bad move in itself, but it leaves the b5 square open, and the next move is easy to get wrong. } 4. e3 Nc6 $2 { Develops, but c7 is guarded only by the queen, and the knight on b5 will land on c7 with check. } 5. Nb5 { Threatens Nc7+, which forks the king and the rook on a8. } 5... a6 $2 { Attacks the knight, but ignores c7. } 6. Nc7+ Kd7 7. Nxa8 { White has won a whole rook. } *
